Z||000000||jch82||04-10-2001||10:51 PM||||I have my entire interior tore out at the moment so I figure now is as good a time as any to fix the cruise and e-brake.<P>Is there anything in particular I should check out that might usually go wrong??<P>Thanks for everything! This forum is great!<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bob Englert||04-10-2001||11:01 PM||||The cruise problem could be a whole host of things.  The factory manual has about 10 pages of wiring diagrams and a troubleshooting matrix to check out the entire system.  Some of the possible problems include:<P>1) electrical problem (no power), fuse, switch, wiring...<BR>2) vac servo or ecm problem.<BR>3) vac leak, rusted out vac res (coffee can)<BR>4) brake and clutch (if equipped) switch problem.<P>I think Rodney Dickman sells reprints of the cruise control section of the Helms (factory manual).  I highly recommend it, there is just too many possible parts that could go wrong.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
